                  "evidence_type": "MANUAL_CURATION",
                  "notes": "Re-grounded from CHEBI:150903 (an unrelated trisaccharide glycoside) (#263). Disodium succinate has no CHEBI entry (checked OAK CHEBI sqlite), so the record takes its CAS-RN as identifier with a narrowMatch to the parent acid, following the established cas: pattern (MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md Section 3). CAS-RN 150-90-3 was already correct.",
                  "source": "MIM curation (#263)"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                  "notes": "Sodium succinate dibasic is a hydrate/salt with its own CAS and no exact ChEBI term; anchored to the parent CHEBI:15741 'succinic acid' by narrowMatch per MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md Section 3 step 2. Disodium succinate has no CHEBI entry; nearest parent is the free acid. Re-grounded from CHEBI:150903 (an unrelated glycoside) in #263.",
                  "source": "reground_263"
                },
                {
                  "evidence_type": "DATABASE_MATCH",
                  "notes": "narrowMatch parent CHEBI:15741 ('succinic acid') -> CHEBI:63675 ('sodium succinate (anhydrous)'). The record is the disodium salt ('dibasic') but was parented to the free acid, so the counterion was discarded. Its own cas_rn 150-90-3 — independent of the ChEBI mapping under test — is registered by ChEBI against CHEBI:63675, whose formula C4H4O4.2Na is the dibasic salt the label names. The record stays cas-primary per MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 step 2; only the parent moves.",
                  "source": "MIM curation (#320)"
                }
